   "subject": "quantifying the robustness of causal inferences: upcoming talks/workshops at U of Minnesota on Sept 26 (12:30-4 central time) and at Northwestern on October 4 (1-5 central time)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" size=\"4\">In case you are in the neighborhood and would like to stop by ...</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" size=\"4\"><b><br></b></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" size=\"4\"><b>Talk at U of Minnesota Sept 26:</b></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" size=\"4\"><b><br></b></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\">Quantifying What it Would Take to Change an Inference: <u></u><u></u></font></span></b></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Toward a Pragmatic Sociology</span></b><b><u></u><u></u></b></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u><font size=\"4\"> </font><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Pragmatic public policy informed by\r\nevidence requires one to make inferences from data.  But statistical\r\ninferences may be challenged because of uncontrolled bias.  There may be\r\nbias due to uncontrolled confounding variables or non-random selection into a\r\nsample.  We will answer the question about what it would take to change an\r\ninference by formalizing the sources of bias and quantifying the discourse\r\nabout causal inferences in terms of those sources.  For example, we will\r\ntransform challenges such as “But the inference of an effect of kindergarten\r\nretention on achievement might not be valid because of pre-existing differences\r\nbetween promoted and retained students” to questions such as “How much bias\r\nmust there have been due to uncontrolled pre-existing differences to make the\r\ninference invalid?”  We will also generate statements such as “An omitted\r\nvariable would have to be correlated at rrr with retention and with achievement\r\nto invalidate the inference.” Calculations will be presented using an app: </span><a href=\"http://konfound-it.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://konfound-it.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3h5mAXCNRixn8wPcMFZhEB\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:windowtext\">http://konfound-it.com</span></a><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> as well as commands in STATA and R.  Ultimately the\r\napproach leads to pragmatic sociology, informing action by quantifying the\r\nconditions that would invalidate inferences supporting that action.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\">Kenneth A. Frank, Michigan State\r\nUniversity<u></u><u></u></font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\">Konfound-it.com   \r\n#konfoundit<u></u><u></u></font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><u></u><font size=\"4\"> </font><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\">12:30-1:30 pm<u></u><u></u></font></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">September 26, 2019 </span><u></u><u></u></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font size=\"4\">325 Education Sciences<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">based on </span><a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/Quantifying%20What%20it%20Would%20Take%20to%20Change%20an%20Inference%20--%20Toward%20a%20Pragmatic%20Sociology%20final.pptx\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,153);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/Quantifying%2520What%2520it%2520Would%2520Take%2520to%2520Change%2520an%2520Inference%2520--%2520Toward%2520a%2520Pragmatic%2520Sociology%2520final.pptx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Uqp-2_NH_iAcv2A0qvy2_\">Quantifying What it Would Take to Change an Inference: Toward a Pragmatic Sociology (ASA Duncan lecture August 2018)</a><span style=\"color:rgb(48,130,152);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> 1 hour</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,130,152);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\">Then there will be more of workshop and discussion from 2-4.  This will be based on:</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,130,152);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(79,129,189)\"><a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%20the%20robustness%20of%20causal%20inferences%20combined%20frameworks%202.pptx\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,153);text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%2520the%2520robustness%2520of%2520causal%2520inferences%2520combined%2520frameworks%25202.pptx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1AhWvY_WmuTEMuITYoHyxZ\"><span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:none\">powerpoint</span></span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:none\"> for combined frameworks</span></a></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(48,130,152)\"> 3 hours (<a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%20the%20robustness%20of%20causal%20inferences%20combined%20frameworks.pdf\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,153)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%2520the%2520robustness%2520of%2520causal%2520inferences%2520combined%2520frameworks.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12cKQXuPPVkAxR30yvaEc-\">pdf</a>)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,130,152);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\" color=\"#000000\">---</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Northwestern Oct 4 from 1-5pm: </span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif\">Workshop:</span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif\"> </span><i><span style=\"font-family:&quot;TimesNewRomanPSMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">What\r\nwould it take to Change your Inference? Quantifying the Robustness of Causal\r\nInferences</span></i></font></p><h3 style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><font size=\"4\" color=\"#000000\"><u></u><u></u></font></h3><h3 style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;TimesNewRomanPSMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#333333\">If you’re interested,\r\nplease RSVP directly to Ken Frank: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kenf...@msu.edu</a></span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">. </span><u></u><u></u></font></h3><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><font size=\"4\"><em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">Motivation</span></em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><br>\r\nStatistical inferences are often challenged because of uncontrolled bias. There\r\nmay be bias due to uncontrolled confounding variables or non-random selection\r\ninto a sample. We will answer the question about what it would take to change\r\nan inference by formalizing the sources of bias and quantifying the discourse\r\nabout causal inferences in terms of those sources. For example, we will\r\ntransform challenges such as “But the inference of a treatment effect might not\r\nbe valid because of pre-existing differences between the treatment groups” to\r\nquestions such as “How much bias must there have been due to uncontrolled\r\npre-existing differences to make the inference invalid?” “QQQ% of the cases\r\nwould have to be replaced with cases with no treatment effect to change the\r\ninference.”</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;box-sizing:border-box\"><font size=\"4\"><em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">Approaches</span></em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><br>\r\nIn part I we will use Rubin’s causal model to interpret how much bias there\r\nmust be to invalidate an inference in terms of replacing observed cases with\r\ncounterfactual cases or cases from an unsampled population. In part II, we will\r\nquantify the robustness of causal inferences in terms of correlations\r\nassociated with unobserved variables or in unsampled populations. Calculations\r\nfor bivariate and multivariate analysis will be presented using an app: <a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=http-3A__konfound-2Dit.com_&amp;d=DwMFAg&amp;c=nE__W8dFE-shTxStwXtp0A&amp;r=F4oW3nXJKTAziDLTsgnr9A&amp;m=tTgkUiXmiyzMSaXbIOq7Nc2xdpoXFG_tKfFuV3XYn2o&amp;s=vnvqy6IPjT-knVFXpuAZYm5IiApvS861BcbiLp3DgKA&amp;e=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u%3Dhttp-3A__konfound-2Dit.com_%26d%3DDwMFAg%26c%3DnE__W8dFE-shTxStwXtp0A%26r%3DF4oW3nXJKTAziDLTsgnr9A%26m%3DtTgkUiXmiyzMSaXbIOq7Nc2xdpoXFG_tKfFuV3XYn2o%26s%3Dvnvqy6IPjT-knVFXpuAZYm5IiApvS861BcbiLp3DgKA%26e%3D&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jryu-9uAbvRUGcpZzSz-j\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,122,183)\">http://konfound-it.com</span></a> as\r\nwell as macros in STATA and R and a spreadsheet for calculating indices\r\n[KonFound-it!].</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;box-sizing:border-box\"><font size=\"4\"><em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">Format</span></em><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><br>\r\nThe format will be a mixture of presentation, individual exploration, and group\r\nwork. Participants may include graduate students and professors, although\r\nparticipants should be comfortable with basic regression. For best results,\r\nparticipants should bring their own laptop, or be willing to work with another\r\nstudent who has a laptop. Participants may choose to bring an example of an\r\ninference from a published study or their own work, as well as data analyses\r\nthey are currently conducting.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;box-sizing:border-box\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">The\r\nworkshop will be provided by <strong>Ken\r\nFrank</strong> MSU Foundation Professor of Sociometrics in\r\nMeasurement and Quantitative Methods at Michigan State University in Counseling,\r\nEducational Psychology and Special Education.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif\"><font size=\"4\">based on:</font></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(79,129,189)\"><a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%20the%20robustness%20of%20causal%20inferences%20combined%20frameworks%202.pptx\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,153);text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%2520the%2520robustness%2520of%2520causal%2520inferences%2520combined%2520frameworks%25202.pptx&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1AhWvY_WmuTEMuITYoHyxZ\"><span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:none\">powerpoint</span></span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:none\"> for combined frameworks</span></a></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:rgb(48,130,152)\"> 3 hours (<a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%20the%20robustness%20of%20causal%20inferences%20combined%20frameworks.pdf\" style=\"color:rgb(0,102,153)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/quantifying%2520the%2520robustness%2520of%2520causal%2520inferences%2520combined%2520frameworks.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw12cKQXuPPVkAxR30yvaEc-\">pdf</a>)</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><b><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif\">Background Reading</span></b><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(58,136,254)\"><a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_What-2520would-2520it-2520take-2520to-2520Change-2520an-2520Inference-2520published.docx&amp;d=DwMGaQ&amp;c=yHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws&amp;r=UzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k&amp;m=M6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8&amp;s=9VWlRalyRWEgYfcs_gz4lp9eJdKvj5a0xXgF23L0r4c&amp;e=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u%3Dhttps-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_What-2520would-2520it-2520take-2520to-2520Change-2520an-2520Inference-2520published.docx%26d%3DDwMGaQ%26c%3DyHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws%26r%3DUzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k%26m%3DM6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8%26s%3D9VWlRalyRWEgYfcs_gz4lp9eJdKvj5a0xXgF23L0r4c%26e%3D&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PeXhL-llL7JLqr9J2kEy6\">Frank, K.A., Maroulis, S., Duong, M., and Kelcey, B.\r\n2013.  What would it take to Change an <span>Inference?:</span> Using Rubin’s Causal Model to Interpret the Robustness of Causal\r\nInferences.   <i>Education, Evaluation and Policy Analysis</i>. <span style=\"border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\"> Vol 35: 437-460.</span></a></span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font size=\"4\"> </font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT,serif;color:rgb(58,136,254)\"><a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_papers_Does-2520NBPTS-2520Certification-2520Affect-2520the-2520Number-2520of-2520Colleagues-2520a-2520Teacher-2520Helps-2520with-2520Instructional-2520Matters-2520acceptance-2520version-25202.doc&amp;d=DwMGaQ&amp;c=yHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws&amp;r=UzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k&amp;m=M6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8&amp;s=YEqDAY9RMQZ_mtGIDmQ63345i5aKS4usrv5nDWl9dtc&amp;e=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u%3Dhttps-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_papers_Does-2520NBPTS-2520Certification-2520Affect-2520the-2520Number-2520of-2520Colleagues-2520a-2520Teacher-2520Helps-2520with-2520Instructional-2520Matters-2520acceptance-2520version-25202.doc%26d%3DDwMGaQ%26c%3DyHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws%26r%3DUzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k%26m%3DM6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8%26s%3DYEqDAY9RMQZ_mtGIDmQ63345i5aKS4usrv5nDWl9dtc%26e%3D&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2YISuyi2L1cJRXI-gXWp_B\">Frank, K.A., Gary Sykes, Dorothea Anagnostopoulos,\r\nMarisa <span>Cannata</span>, Linda Chard, Ann Krause, Raven McCrory. 2008.\r\nExtended Influence: National Board Certified Teachers as Help\r\nProviders. Education, Evaluation, and Policy Analysis.  Vol\r\n30(1): 3-30.</a></span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u><font size=\"4\"> </font><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<font size=\"4\"><u></u><u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<u></u><u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<u></u><u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<u></u><u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<u></u><u></u>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_papers_impact-2520of-2520a-2520confounding-2520variable.pdf&amp;d=DwMGaQ&amp;c=yHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws&amp;r=UzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k&amp;m=M6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8&amp;s=tWnyTuHjSrAy7uF1qbfzfuL-2J6-UcyL7z2sgmSK6Ho&amp;e=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u%3Dhttps-3A__msu.edu_-7Ekenfrank_papers_impact-2520of-2520a-2520confounding-2520variable.pdf%26d%3DDwMGaQ%26c%3DyHlS04HhBraes5BQ9ueu5zKhE7rtNXt_d012z2PA6ws%26r%3DUzNSaBXa2smBXDA76d2iPpAK5DnTp8JfsCv0NOpyz5k%26m%3DM6urIpFffyoQow2_nqlzbjnUFbQsKDmpfrJTG6SRaw8%26s%3DtWnyTuHjSrAy7uF1qbfzfuL-2J6-UcyL7z2sgmSK6Ho%26e%3D&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244518024000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0LQPkBS3iKq4b9m3j5R5SS\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;TimesNewRomanPSMT&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#0056d6\"><font size=\"4\">Frank, K. 2000. &quot;Impact\r\nof a Confounding Variable on the Inference of a Regression Coefficient.&quot; Sociological\r\nMethods and Research, 29(2), 147-194</font></span></a><u></u><u></u></p></div>"
